record lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.at-handoff-knowledge-validate-withheld-its/1 : papercut {
    title "At handoff, knowledge.validate withheld its entire 8.5k-token result…"
    state verified
    statement """
        At handoff, knowledge.validate withheld its entire 8.5k-token result and suggested narrower arguments even though the tool exposes no scope/filter argument; diagnosing required the separate `akr check` CLI (the protocol's `knowledge.validate` name is not a CLI subcommand). A summarized diagnostics mode would make the required handoff check actionable.
        """
    observed_at git:ef8b70669f02df887a959aafe62ac996691c9ef3
    about "akr"
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.correcting-an-inaccurate-papercut-via-knowledge/1 : papercut {
    title "Correcting an inaccurate papercut via knowledge.supersede failed…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Correcting an inaccurate papercut via knowledge.supersede failed because the connected workspace vocabulary 0.1 does not support the tool schema's `new_key` option. The correction had to reuse the original key instead of creating a clearer replacement key.
        """
    observed_at git:ef8b70669f02df887a959aafe62ac996691c9ef3
    about "akr"
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.creating-the-finalization-work-record-failed/1 : papercut {
    title "Creating the finalization work record failed because `depends_on`…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Creating the finalization work record failed because `depends_on` cannot reference a completed work record, but the propose schema does not identify which relation should capture historical provenance. The write was retried with only the live decision dependency.
        """
    observed_at git:ef8b70669f02df887a959aafe62ac996691c9ef3
    about "akr"
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.imported-lege-ecosystem-perf-audit-work-records/1 : papercut {
    title "Imported lege-ecosystem-perf audit work records (2026-08-05) are stale…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Imported lege-ecosystem-perf audit work records (2026-08-05) are stale vs code: their P1/Phase-1..3 defects (nonzero tile origins disabling optimized DWT, per-row 9/7 scratch, full planar staging, missing packed Rgbx8/Bgra8 formats) are already fixed in lege-codecs/jp2lam. Determining 'unfinished' work required reading source per-item since ledger states are all still 'proposed'. Consider reconciling/closing those imported records against the implementation.
        """
    observed_at git:5780178af9f0d10bc4a8457259dfa141c2f804de
    author "fugu"
    created_at 2026-08-06
}

record lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.knowledge-context-withheld-a-4-1k-token-bundle/1 : papercut {
    title "knowledge.context withheld a 4.1k-token bundle even though I requested…"
    state verified
    statement """
        knowledge.context withheld a 4.1k-token bundle even though I requested a 16k budget, then advised requesting fewer tokens. The MCP response ceiling is lower than the tool's advertised budget parameter, so context had to be retried with narrower paths.
        """
    observed_at git:ef8b70669f02df887a959aafe62ac996691c9ef3
    about "akr"
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.running-cargo-fmt-check-from-lege-pdf-render/1 : papercut {
    title "Running `cargo fmt --check` from `lege-pdf/render` failed with…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Running `cargo fmt --check` from `lege-pdf/render` failed with “Failed to find targets” because that directory is not a usable Cargo formatting root even though renderer crates are nested beneath it. The verification workflow needs to point rustfmt/cargo at the concrete crate or the external tool manifest.
        """
    observed_at git:ef8b70669f02df887a959aafe62ac996691c9ef3
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.the-targeted-renderer-image-clippy-check-is/1 : papercut {
    title "The targeted renderer/image clippy check is blocked by an unrelated…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The targeted renderer/image clippy check is blocked by an unrelated existing `-D clippy::expect-used` violation in `lege-pdf/render/crates/pdf-document/src/pages.rs:594`, reached through `pdf-cli` dependencies. Renderer/image tests pass, but the documented clippy gate cannot complete until that pre-existing lint is resolved or the check is scoped differently.
        """
    observed_at git:ef8b70669f02df887a959aafe62ac996691c9ef3
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.while-recording-the-renderer-decision-knowledge/1 : papercut {
    title "While recording the renderer decision, knowledge.propose rejected a…"
    state verified
    statement """
        While recording the renderer decision, knowledge.propose rejected a dotted decision topic even though the key is dot-delimited; the topic segment syntax was not apparent from the tool schema, so the write had to be retried with a single hyphenated segment. The response also warned that the connected MCP vocabulary 0.2 is newer than the workspace build vocabulary 0.1.
        """
    observed_at git:ef8b70669f02df887a959aafe62ac996691c9ef3
    about "akr"
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.while-reproducing-the-structures-pdf-mrc/1 : papercut {
    title "While reproducing the Structures.pdf MRC profile, the performance…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        While reproducing the Structures.pdf MRC profile, the performance handoff labels the 2222x3191 run as scale 2.0833333, but the supplied 444.4x638.2-point page produces 926x1330 at that scale and 2222x3191 at scale 5.0. Benchmark records should store both requested scale and resulting dimensions so comparisons cannot silently mix them.
        """
    observed_at git:ef8b70669f02df887a959aafe62ac996691c9ef3
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

